 I was  working a large telecommunications  company one day doing a seminar and API  design best practice and they kept  stumbling they were trying to design  their their texting API  right there SMS API and they kept having  like a hundred data fields in there and  I kept saying to myself I don't I'm not  an expert in this field but it seems  like you've got a sender a timestamp  content and an array of receivers so  like four fields something like that I  mean whatever it is it's closer to four  than it is a hundred and I said to them  why do you think it's a hundred like why  I mean you're the experts but why is  this they said well you know we just  updated this system to seven point two  point eight but nobody cares right no  but nobody should ever care or know  about that information right with API is  you got to think outside not not inside  somebody outside of our organization  outside of our department whatever what  are they coming to us for like why do  they come here why do they come to us  and make that as easy to consume as  possible make your your best goods on  offer as a super consumable API that's  the way to start thinking about  consumption is the other parts of the  business that come to us why do they  come to us what's what's our core  offering for them our customers what's  the main reason they come to us how can  I make that as easy to consume as  possible instead of what are the  advantages or limitations of my back-end  systems or what kind of version or  vendor I've got on my back-end stuff and  one question I get all the time is Brian  you keep telling us not to think of the  api's as a project right think of as a  product but we're starting with a  project are you know are we wrong it's  just the wrong thing to do and of course  not you've you often in a big  organization will have a project that's  funded that's staffed if it has a  charter that's on your portfolio that's  great that's a perfect way it's a  perfect opportunity to introduce these  technologies and introduce this  methodology as long as you're aware that  this goes well beyond that project right  api's should be the center of every  project you do your API platform should  span lines of business and be across the  entire brand as long as you go into that  single project with that mindset you  won't make those you know I'm a lifelong  Software Architect those thousand  decisions that you make none of which by  themselves are critical but if you make  them all in the wrong direction you're  going to end up at a very different  outcome and so if you think of this is  not just for this project but this is  the future of the company  then the project is a great way to get  started right and and to me after these  kinds of sessions some people say well  Brian I know your your you love  linguistics you love language things  like that is this just fundamentally a  semantic issue and I truly don't believe  that you know any of you who have built  software which I assume as most of you  know that it's not just you know what  color the button is and where it goes on  the screen there are thousand questions  and design decisions that we have to do  along the creation of a product and if  we make all those decisions in a way  that thinks of this in a very inside  first traditional 20th century kind of  mindset the result is going to be  unfortunate what we see all over the app  stores right now which is traditional  companies just kind of looking silly  with their apps how far behind they are  graphically and usability and we're all  friends right we all have have companies  that we're customers of and we're  frustrated with their apps and why can't  this be more like you know some Silicon  Valley startups fantastic glamorous app  and I think that's the harm I think the  harm is thinking that what got you there  in the 20th century is what's going to  win in the 21st century when it  empirically we know that that's not true  right and so not focusing on the  experience the customer experience not  focusing on speed right not focusing on  working across organizational trust  boundaries I don't think that's  semantics at all and I think that's that  fundamentally like statistically will  lead you to situations that are  conducive to failing in the 21st century  just as if you are API centric and  you're thinking of things in terms of  products and consumed ability and  customer experience it doesn't guarantee  success but it creates conditions that  are conducive to success in the current  digital app based 21st century  marketplace that we all have to compete  in whether we like it or not in every  region of the globe and every vertical  we're all doing business in 2018 and  this is simply what our employees our  developers our partners and our  customers have come to expect from us so  I think that's all the questions that we  had and I know sometimes it's hard when  you're on the spot here to think of a  question right now if you think of one  when you're taking a shower tomorrow  morning and  you know I wish I'd asked Brian this  question feel free to ping us anytime  reach out to us we'd be happy to talk we  love talking about this stuff and we get  very fired up talking about this stuff  and otherwise we hope that you'll tune  in to our next next week next Tuesday  for the next cloud on-air webinar my  name is Brian Pagano come to you from  Google cloud thank you so much for your  time today

